1
00:00:05,500 --> 00:00:12,600
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

2
00:00:39,167 --> 00:00:41,000
[SCREAMING IN PAIN]

3
00:00:42,133 --> 00:00:43,467
[TIRES SCREECHING]

4
00:00:45,467 --> 00:00:46,800
- [ENGINE REVVING]
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

5
00:00:55,933 --> 00:00:57,300
[TIRES SCREECH]

6
00:00:58,100 --> 00:00:59,900
[ENGINES REVVING]

7
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:01,067
[TRUCK HORN BLARES]

8
00:01:01,200 --> 00:01:02,400
[LOUD CRASH]

9
00:01:02,533 --> 00:01:04,833
[TIRES SCREECHING]

10
00:01:06,133 --> 00:01:07,567
<i>- Stop!
- [GUNSHOTS]</i>

11
00:01:10,467 --> 00:01:11,833
[FIREWORKS EXPLODING]

12
00:01:13,467 --> 00:01:17,367
[METAL RODS CLANGING]

13
00:01:17,500 --> 00:01:19,500
- [ENGINE REVVING]
- [BUS HORN HONKS]

14
00:01:20,467 --> 00:01:22,333
[GLASS SHATTERING]

15
00:01:22,467 --> 00:01:25,033
- [TIRES SCREECHING]
- [LOUD CRASH]

16
00:01:25,833 --> 00:01:28,700
[ENGINES REVVING]

17
00:01:30,467 --> 00:01:31,867
[TIRES SCREECHING]

18
00:01:32,633 --> 00:01:35,300
[TIRES SCREECHING]

19
00:01:35,467 --> 00:01:36,367
[GUNSHOTS]

20
00:01:36,500 --> 00:01:38,033
[TIRES SCREECHING]

21
00:01:38,167 --> 00:01:39,100
- [TRUCK HORN HONKS]
- [LOUD CRASH]

22
00:01:39,233 --> 00:01:40,967
[TIRES SCREECHING]

23
00:01:46,367 --> 00:01:47,567
<i> The law is the law.</i>

24
00:01:47,700 --> 00:01:50,467
<i>If someone breaks it,
they must be held accountable!</i>

25
00:01:50,600 --> 00:01:53,633
<i>There are things that we do
that are often</i>

26
00:01:53,733 --> 00:01:57,133
not in accordance with the law.
<i> But they're necessary.</i>

27
00:01:57,233 --> 00:01:59,833
The mission was still a success.
<i> We caught Mr. Chan.</i>

28
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:01,067
<i> We are one team.</i>

29
00:02:01,233 --> 00:02:02,700
<i>We will continue to support
each other until the end.</i>

30
00:02:02,833 --> 00:02:06,700
<i>- I'll get back at them, Ma.
- Forget about Mr. Chan for now.</i>

31
00:02:06,833 --> 00:02:10,367
I'm not talking about Mr. Chan.
<i> But the one who shot me!</i>

32
00:02:10,500 --> 00:02:11,567
<i> Someone else was there</i>

33
00:02:11,700 --> 00:02:13,200
<i>that made it easier for us
to catch Mr. Chan.</i>

34
00:02:13,333 --> 00:02:14,400
<i> The question is, who was it?</i>

35
00:02:14,567 --> 00:02:16,167
<i>- Here's the gold.
- It's all here.</i>

36
00:02:16,267 --> 00:02:17,667
<i> In a moment of temptation,</i>

37
00:02:17,767 --> 00:02:22,067
<i>a person's true character
and principles show.</i>

38
00:02:22,200 --> 00:02:24,433
<i>I have the money for
Papa's medicine and surgery.</i>

39
00:02:24,567 --> 00:02:26,667
<i>Thank you so much
for keeping your promise.</i>

40
00:02:26,800 --> 00:02:28,333
<i> The surgery was successful.</i>

41
00:02:28,467 --> 00:02:30,667
<i>Let's just wait for him
to wake up.</i>

42
00:02:33,200 --> 00:02:34,233
[JAIL GATE CREAKS]

43
00:02:34,367 --> 00:02:36,833
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

44
00:02:36,933 --> 00:02:37,867
[POLICE] Sign here.

45
00:02:39,200 --> 00:02:40,433
Mr. Chan!

46
00:02:41,433 --> 00:02:44,533
Victor! Nice to see you,
but not here.

47
00:02:44,700 --> 00:02:45,600
How did you get caught?

48
00:02:45,733 --> 00:02:48,533
This agent, lady agent,
very good acting!

49
00:02:48,733 --> 00:02:51,200
She fooled me!
Pretend to be my buyer!

50
00:02:51,300 --> 00:02:53,767
- Which agent?
- Sam. Sam...

51
00:02:54,567 --> 00:02:56,433
Jacinto! Sam Jacinto!

52
00:02:56,567 --> 00:02:58,033
That woman's taking us out
one by one.

53
00:02:58,133 --> 00:03:00,367
She won't stop until
I get pinned on this case.

54
00:03:00,967 --> 00:03:02,967
No, Victor.
She's not the reason.

55
00:03:03,100 --> 00:03:04,133
She did not catch me.

56
00:03:04,267 --> 00:03:05,867
This guy? Long hair guy,

57
00:03:06,000 --> 00:03:07,033
- jacket, he caught me.
- Stay here, stay here.

58
00:03:07,133 --> 00:03:09,700
- Go away from there.
- Not Jacinto, not the girl.

59
00:03:09,800 --> 00:03:11,133
Go inside.

60
00:03:13,800 --> 00:03:15,533
- Hey! Hey! Hey, you!
- [JAIL GATE CLANGING]

61
00:03:15,633 --> 00:03:16,967
I need my phone call!

62
00:03:18,167 --> 00:03:19,367
[VICTOR] It's him again.

63
00:03:19,500 --> 00:03:21,567
<i>Why is he so dead set
on catching us?</i>

64
00:03:21,767 --> 00:03:23,100
<i> Once I get out of here,</i>

65
00:03:23,267 --> 00:03:27,567
<i>I'll find that bastard,
and make him pay.</i>

66
00:03:27,700 --> 00:03:31,667
[CHAN] I need to talk my lawyer!
I want call! Hey!

67
00:03:32,500 --> 00:03:33,433
Hey!

68
00:03:33,600 --> 00:03:34,567
[JAIL GATE CLANGING]

69
00:03:34,700 --> 00:03:38,433
Hey, hey! Hey! Hey!

70
00:03:39,267 --> 00:03:40,167
[DEBORAH] Mariano.

71
00:03:41,267 --> 00:03:42,167
Just a minute.

72
00:03:44,467 --> 00:03:45,667
Go on.

73
00:03:46,767 --> 00:03:52,800
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

74
00:03:52,933 --> 00:03:57,500
After 20 years,
Ricardo and I will meet again.

75
00:03:58,500 --> 00:04:01,433
I'll show him the new Mariano.

76
00:04:01,533 --> 00:04:04,633
I am one with you
in confronting Ricardo.

77
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:07,600
I'm also angry
with his daughter.

78
00:04:08,500 --> 00:04:14,600
I'm angry with all aggravations
affecting our business.

79
00:04:16,367 --> 00:04:17,667
However, are you truly ready

80
00:04:17,800 --> 00:04:21,100
to start a war
against the police?

81
00:04:21,200 --> 00:04:23,267
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

82
00:04:23,367 --> 00:04:25,633
I'm not scared of them.

83
00:04:28,733 --> 00:04:31,667
Once we start a war,
there's no turning back.

84
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:35,200
Do you really want
to do this now?

85
00:04:35,333 --> 00:04:37,500
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

86
00:04:37,667 --> 00:04:39,633
Now, when Victor's in jail...

87
00:04:40,700 --> 00:04:42,867
And Lucas is still healing?

88
00:04:46,067 --> 00:04:47,133
Don't worry.

89
00:04:48,733 --> 00:04:50,967
I'll do what is right.

90
00:04:53,600 --> 00:05:00,733
[MUSIC INTENSIFYING]

91
00:05:03,967 --> 00:05:04,567
[MUSIC ENDS]

92
00:05:04,700 --> 00:05:06,200
[CRICKETS CHIRPING IN DISTANCE]

93
00:05:06,367 --> 00:05:08,233
[LINE RINGING]

94
00:05:08,367 --> 00:05:12,033
[PHONE RINGING]

95
00:05:12,767 --> 00:05:13,833
[PHONE BEEPS]

96
00:05:14,367 --> 00:05:15,333
Yes, General?

97
00:05:15,433 --> 00:05:17,000
<i> Good evening, Dir. Delgado.</i>

98
00:05:17,100 --> 00:05:20,233
I would like to talk to you
about Samantha and the NCIA.

99
00:05:20,367 --> 00:05:21,500
<i> What about...</i>

100
00:05:21,600 --> 00:05:24,167
the NCIA and Sam would you
like to talk about?

101
00:05:24,300 --> 00:05:25,700
<i> Well, Director, I understand.</i>

102
00:05:26,233 --> 00:05:28,500
I can see that you have
a lot of confidence in Samantha.

103
00:05:29,100 --> 00:05:31,533
Because you let her handle
the gold smuggling case.

104
00:05:32,067 --> 00:05:34,567
<i>But I heard she's up against
a very powerful syndicate.</i>

105
00:05:34,733 --> 00:05:37,567
General, she's like a
daughter to me.

106
00:05:37,733 --> 00:05:39,700
<i> Let me be frank, General.</i>

107
00:05:40,333 --> 00:05:42,133
You're being harsh on her.

108
00:05:42,567 --> 00:05:43,800
Harsh? What do you mean harsh?

109
00:05:44,233 --> 00:05:49,133
She's under too much pressure
to please you,

110
00:05:49,733 --> 00:05:52,300
<i>so much that
she's losing focus at work.</i>

111
00:05:53,067 --> 00:05:56,133
There are things
she could have fixed

112
00:05:56,267 --> 00:05:57,200
<i> or corrected, but...</i>

113
00:05:57,333 --> 00:05:59,600
instead she worries
about earning your approval.

114
00:05:59,733 --> 00:06:01,800
<i> Such as? Director, please.</i>

115
00:06:01,933 --> 00:06:04,400
Please tell me, because
I just want to know if...

116
00:06:04,900 --> 00:06:07,433
the blame is on me,
or if I'm crossing the line.

117
00:06:07,600 --> 00:06:08,667
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

118
00:06:08,800 --> 00:06:12,633
Sam acted on her own,
even though I forbade it,

119
00:06:12,767 --> 00:06:18,467
to catch those connected
to the syndicate.

120
00:06:18,833 --> 00:06:21,333
<i>A shootout broke out.
And, uh...</i>

121
00:06:21,467 --> 00:06:22,900
one of them was injured.

122
00:06:23,000 --> 00:06:26,100
But they were all safe
and caught the criminal.

123
00:06:26,267 --> 00:06:28,333
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

124
00:06:28,467 --> 00:06:29,900
Thank you for telling me.

125
00:06:30,033 --> 00:06:31,167
<i> General...</i>

126
00:06:31,633 --> 00:06:34,833
Sam needs a father
who will guide her.

127
00:06:35,533 --> 00:06:37,633
<i> She desperately needs you.</i>

128
00:06:38,133 --> 00:06:39,267
Thank you.

129
00:06:41,200 --> 00:06:42,133
[PHONE BEEPS]

130
00:06:42,867 --> 00:06:44,133
[MANNY] Boss.

131
00:06:44,300 --> 00:06:47,433
I've already had the clubhouse
manager sign the NDA form.

132
00:06:47,567 --> 00:06:48,667
Whatever you discuss here,

133
00:06:48,800 --> 00:06:50,200
it's gonna be confidential.

134
00:06:51,400 --> 00:06:52,333
Good.

135
00:06:53,333 --> 00:06:54,467
And by the way, Manny...

136
00:06:54,633 --> 00:06:56,167
Double the security.

137
00:06:56,800 --> 00:06:58,867
I don't trust the person
we're meeting later.

138
00:06:59,367 --> 00:07:00,333
No problem, sir.

139
00:07:01,200 --> 00:07:01,967
Let's go, Toto.

140
00:07:02,133 --> 00:07:06,433
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

141
00:07:06,567 --> 00:07:07,467
[MUSIC ENDS]

142
00:07:07,800 --> 00:07:08,933
[MAX] Hi, Ma.

143
00:07:09,733 --> 00:07:10,633
Where's Dad?

144
00:07:10,800 --> 00:07:12,000
[ISOBEL] I...

145
00:07:12,467 --> 00:07:13,333
...don't know.

146
00:07:13,467 --> 00:07:14,600
[INHALES DEEPLY]

147
00:07:14,733 --> 00:07:16,733
He left without telling me
where he was going.

148
00:07:18,200 --> 00:07:19,200
[SIGHS]

149
00:07:22,600 --> 00:07:23,800
Ma...

150
00:07:26,500 --> 00:07:27,733
I'm sorry.

151
00:07:28,000 --> 00:07:29,967
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

152
00:07:30,067 --> 00:07:32,700
I know I've failed this family
in many ways.

153
00:07:32,833 --> 00:07:33,967
[INHALES SHARPLY]

154
00:07:35,267 --> 00:07:36,300
And recently,

155
00:07:37,067 --> 00:07:38,467
things have been such a mess.

156
00:07:39,200 --> 00:07:40,167
[MAX SNIFFLES]

157
00:07:40,333 --> 00:07:42,367
And I want you to know...

158
00:07:42,700 --> 00:07:44,900
that I understand
where you're coming from.

159
00:07:45,033 --> 00:07:46,633
- [SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]
- [INHALES DEEPLY]

160
00:07:46,733 --> 00:07:49,467
You know, I've delivered
the world peace answer

161
00:07:50,133 --> 00:07:52,600
in pageants
so many times before.

162
00:07:53,033 --> 00:07:56,167
But this time, I really mean it.

163
00:07:56,433 --> 00:07:58,333
I want peace...

164
00:07:58,867 --> 00:08:00,333
...for our family.

165
00:08:01,233 --> 00:08:02,533
Don't worry, Ma.

166
00:08:02,700 --> 00:08:03,933
I'll make it up to you.

167
00:08:04,067 --> 00:08:05,367
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

168
00:08:05,533 --> 00:08:06,867
Actually...

169
00:08:08,467 --> 00:08:10,167
I think I already did.

170
00:08:11,700 --> 00:08:13,000
What do you mean?

171
00:08:14,200 --> 00:08:17,000
Do you remember that woman
from the news?

172
00:08:17,133 --> 00:08:18,933
The wife of the gunshot victim?

173
00:08:19,400 --> 00:08:20,833
I went to see her and...

174
00:08:20,967 --> 00:08:22,567
gave her some money.

175
00:08:22,933 --> 00:08:24,900
You mean, it's already settled?

176
00:08:25,067 --> 00:08:26,033
[MAX] Well, I think...

177
00:08:26,133 --> 00:08:27,900
I think we're getting there.

178
00:08:28,967 --> 00:08:30,700
The family is still being
stubborn, especially the son.

179
00:08:30,800 --> 00:08:32,733
But this woman...

180
00:08:32,900 --> 00:08:34,467
I think I've won her over.

181
00:08:34,600 --> 00:08:37,367
And she can help us
fix this mess.

182
00:08:38,333 --> 00:08:39,433
That's good.

183
00:08:39,567 --> 00:08:42,433
[SOMBER MUSIC CONTINUES]

184
00:08:42,567 --> 00:08:48,367
[ENGINES RUMBLING]

185
00:08:48,500 --> 00:08:49,433
[CAR DOOR CLOSES]

186
00:08:49,567 --> 00:08:51,700
[HURRIED FOOTSTEPS]

187
00:08:51,833 --> 00:08:52,767
[CAR DOOR OPENS]

188
00:08:52,900 --> 00:08:57,400
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

189
00:08:57,600 --> 00:08:59,000
[CAR DOOR CLOSES]

190
00:09:02,100 --> 00:09:04,467
Sir, you can't bring your guns.

191
00:09:04,933 --> 00:09:06,900
[TOTO] Sir Manny,
they're coming up now.

192
00:09:07,033 --> 00:09:08,900
Just leave the big ones.

193
00:09:09,433 --> 00:09:10,433
- Sir.
- Yes, sir.

194
00:09:12,100 --> 00:09:17,900
[UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

195
00:09:18,000 --> 00:09:19,333
Wait a minute.

196
00:09:20,033 --> 00:09:22,933
We have a meeting
with Gen. Ricardo Jacinto.

197
00:09:23,100 --> 00:09:25,000
Are you Mariano Zafra?

198
00:09:25,333 --> 00:09:26,433
I am.

199
00:09:26,600 --> 00:09:28,067
You're the only one allowed in.

200
00:09:28,200 --> 00:09:28,933
No.

201
00:09:29,067 --> 00:09:30,600
We need to stay with him.

202
00:09:30,733 --> 00:09:33,433
Gen. Jacinto's order was clear.

203
00:09:33,533 --> 00:09:36,100
Mariano Zafra's the only one
allowed inside.

204
00:09:37,400 --> 00:09:39,933
It's alright.
Just wait for me here.

205
00:09:41,033 --> 00:09:43,500
Sir, if any problem comes up,
we'll be right here.

206
00:09:44,033 --> 00:09:46,500
Don't worry, he
won't touch me.

207
00:09:46,633 --> 00:09:47,433
Pat him down.

208
00:09:48,467 --> 00:09:49,600
There's no need for that.

209
00:09:50,033 --> 00:09:52,100
[GUN CLATTERS]

210
00:09:53,200 --> 00:09:54,133
Happy now?

211
00:09:55,467 --> 00:09:56,800
Let's go.

212
00:09:57,533 --> 00:10:04,433
[UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

213
00:10:04,600 --> 00:10:06,000
General Jacinto is right there.

214
00:10:11,700 --> 00:10:14,000
[MARIANO] Ricardo.
Long time no see.

215
00:10:17,867 --> 00:10:19,200
It's been a long time.

216
00:10:20,100 --> 00:10:22,500
I can just call you Ricardo,
right?

217
00:10:23,000 --> 00:10:25,467
After all,
we're both retired now.

218
00:10:25,933 --> 00:10:27,300
Call me anything you want.

219
00:10:27,767 --> 00:10:28,633
Sit down.

220
00:10:28,767 --> 00:10:35,633
[UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

221
00:10:38,800 --> 00:10:40,033
What do you want?

222
00:10:40,200 --> 00:10:41,367
[MARIANO] I'll cut to the chase.

223
00:10:41,900 --> 00:10:43,500
You know why I'm here.

224
00:10:44,567 --> 00:10:45,933
As I said before,

225
00:10:46,533 --> 00:10:48,833
I have no control over
my daughter Samantha.

226
00:10:49,533 --> 00:10:52,367
I already talked to her,
but she won't listen.

227
00:10:54,733 --> 00:10:58,667
What does your daughter want?

228
00:10:59,367 --> 00:11:01,900
Does she want money,
cars, a house?

229
00:11:02,033 --> 00:11:04,667
I can give all of that to her!

230
00:11:06,700 --> 00:11:09,600
Not to be arrogant,
but we can give those to her.

231
00:11:09,767 --> 00:11:10,700
But you don't get it.

232
00:11:12,300 --> 00:11:15,533
Bribery won't work on her.

233
00:11:16,833 --> 00:11:19,300
So, this means that
you won't help me?

234
00:11:19,433 --> 00:11:20,300
So you're saying

235
00:11:20,433 --> 00:11:24,033
that Samantha
won't help my son?

236
00:11:31,967 --> 00:11:33,067
I'm sorry.

237
00:11:33,233 --> 00:11:40,267
[UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

238
00:11:43,500 --> 00:11:44,600
You were a General.

239
00:11:46,367 --> 00:11:48,567
You had control over
the whole police force!

240
00:11:48,700 --> 00:11:51,100
Now, you can't even
order around your own child

241
00:11:51,267 --> 00:11:52,300
who holds a low rank?

242
00:11:53,100 --> 00:11:54,267
You useless father!

243
00:11:54,800 --> 00:11:55,733
[THUDS]

244
00:11:56,533 --> 00:11:58,267
Who the hell
do you think you are

245
00:11:58,433 --> 00:11:59,933
to question about how
I raise my daughters?

246
00:12:00,100 --> 00:12:01,900
Your son is a criminal.

247
00:12:02,000 --> 00:12:04,133
You are the reason why
he's in jail right now.

248
00:12:04,933 --> 00:12:06,433
He's just like you.

249
00:12:06,600 --> 00:12:08,433
You've always had
the mindset of a criminal!

250
00:12:13,133 --> 00:12:15,833
This "hoodlum brain"
you're talking about

251
00:12:16,900 --> 00:12:19,500
is the one who helped you get
everything you wanted before!

252
00:12:20,567 --> 00:12:23,467
You gained all of this wealth
because of me!

253
00:12:24,067 --> 00:12:25,700
I hope you never
forgot about that.

254
00:12:26,067 --> 00:12:28,033
Or maybe you need me
to remind you.

255
00:12:28,500 --> 00:12:30,167
And now you're threatening me?

256
00:12:31,733 --> 00:12:33,300
Don't.

257
00:12:33,467 --> 00:12:36,467
Even though I retired,
I'm still a General, Mariano.

258
00:12:37,633 --> 00:12:40,100
I still have my own connections
and influence.

259
00:12:40,200 --> 00:12:42,267
And that's called power.

260
00:12:44,167 --> 00:12:47,533
Was your family
business successful?

261
00:12:48,167 --> 00:12:49,633
Don't mess with me.

262
00:12:51,200 --> 00:12:53,233
Your group and your family
are going to pay for this.

263
00:12:53,733 --> 00:12:55,467
So don't you ever cross me.

264
00:12:56,667 --> 00:12:58,400
This will be the last time
we'll see each other.

265
00:13:03,433 --> 00:13:04,633
- Let's go.
- [GRUNTS]

266
00:13:04,733 --> 00:13:11,533
[UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

267
00:13:21,567 --> 00:13:22,500
Sir.

268
00:13:23,200 --> 00:13:24,500
How did it go?

269
00:13:25,100 --> 00:13:26,167
Let's go.

270
00:13:26,900 --> 00:13:28,400
[RICARDO] Does Mariano think

271
00:13:29,433 --> 00:13:32,167
<i>that he has control over me
because he knows my past?</i>

272
00:13:33,033 --> 00:13:34,667
<i> I won't let that happen.</i>

273
00:13:35,633 --> 00:13:36,933
<i> Come to think of it,</i>

274
00:13:37,067 --> 00:13:38,233
<i> he benefited from this too.</i>

275
00:13:38,367 --> 00:13:39,433
[UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

276
00:13:41,633 --> 00:13:42,367
- I'll fix this.
- [DOOR OPENS]

277
00:13:45,067 --> 00:13:46,133
[CLEARS THROAT] Dad.

278
00:13:46,133 --> 00:13:47,267
Where's Sam?

279
00:13:47,933 --> 00:13:51,400
I don't know.
Maybe she's still at work.

280
00:13:51,533 --> 00:13:55,167
Dad, why do you seem angry?
Where were you?

281
00:13:55,333 --> 00:13:56,700
It doesn't matter where I was.

282
00:13:56,833 --> 00:13:59,233
What's important
is I talk to your sister.

283
00:13:59,333 --> 00:14:00,767
She has crossed the line.

284
00:14:02,100 --> 00:14:04,633
Oh, Ricardo.
What is this about again?

285
00:14:04,800 --> 00:14:09,467
Is there a problem?
Maybe we can fix it together.

286
00:14:09,600 --> 00:14:11,267
I'll handle it, Isobel.

287
00:14:11,400 --> 00:14:14,800
Knowing you, you can't
discipline your daughter.

288
00:14:16,800 --> 00:14:17,967
[RICARDO SIGHS DEEPLY]

289
00:14:25,067 --> 00:14:31,867
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

290
00:14:37,267 --> 00:14:39,100
[YOUNG RICARDO]
<i> File a police report.</i>

291
00:14:39,267 --> 00:14:41,800
<i> Homicide and robbery.</i>

292
00:14:43,000 --> 00:14:45,100
<i>No one else must know
about what happened, Mariano.</i>

293
00:14:46,167 --> 00:14:48,733
<i>We will carry this secret
to our graves.</i>

294
00:14:48,867 --> 00:14:50,300
[YOUNG MARIANO] Yes, sir.
You can count on it.

295
00:14:50,433 --> 00:14:51,900
<i> Sir.</i>

296
00:14:52,033 --> 00:14:56,267
<i>Since Rudy's gone,
can I get my share?</i>

297
00:14:56,433 --> 00:14:58,433
<i> Sure. Take that.</i>

298
00:14:58,600 --> 00:14:59,967
<i> That's your share.</i>

299
00:15:02,467 --> 00:15:04,000
<i> And that's a little bonus.</i>

300
00:15:04,967 --> 00:15:07,533
<i>Sir, don't you think
that's a little unfair to me?</i>

301
00:15:07,667 --> 00:15:09,133
<i> I've done so much for you.</i>

302
00:15:09,300 --> 00:15:11,633
<i>Unfair? Why? Did you
invest money in this?</i>

303
00:15:11,800 --> 00:15:12,867
<i> You didn't.</i>

304
00:15:13,000 --> 00:15:15,433
<i>Mariano, just be thankful
I gave you a share.</i>

305
00:15:16,533 --> 00:15:18,200
Don't forget the police report.

306
00:15:18,333 --> 00:15:25,133
[GRIM MUSIC PLAYING]

307
00:15:30,233 --> 00:15:32,500
<i>I'll make you pay one day,
you bastard.</i>

308
00:15:41,000 --> 00:15:47,700
[GRIM MUSIC CONTINUES]

309
00:15:49,033 --> 00:15:50,800
I know what you're thinking.

310
00:15:50,900 --> 00:15:53,633
You've waited so long for this.

311
00:15:53,733 --> 00:15:57,833
To get back at Ricardo
for everything he did to you.

312
00:15:58,667 --> 00:16:01,533
He abused and belittled me.

313
00:16:01,700 --> 00:16:04,667
But with the little gold
he spared me,

314
00:16:04,767 --> 00:16:07,867
we were able to start
our business and grow it.

315
00:16:09,533 --> 00:16:11,233
You don't have to rush.

316
00:16:12,100 --> 00:16:14,733
Let him think
that he's still in control.

317
00:16:15,600 --> 00:16:16,667
Mm.

318
00:16:16,767 --> 00:16:18,667
You'll have your
glory days soon.

319
00:16:25,767 --> 00:16:29,233
The tides will turn
to our favor.

320
00:16:33,567 --> 00:16:37,533
Why is your dad
in a bad mood again?

321
00:16:37,633 --> 00:16:39,733
For sure, Sam did
something again.

322
00:16:39,900 --> 00:16:41,733
Don't worry, Ma.
I'll talk to Sam.

323
00:16:41,933 --> 00:16:43,200
I just hope she listens

324
00:16:44,133 --> 00:16:46,200
and we don't get
into another fight.

325
00:16:46,300 --> 00:16:47,600
"Another fight?"

326
00:16:47,767 --> 00:16:51,033
I told her off last night
for talking back at Dad.

327
00:16:51,133 --> 00:16:54,767
Goodness!
You're all stressing me out!

328
00:16:55,500 --> 00:16:56,300
There she is.

329
00:16:57,333 --> 00:16:58,367
Hey, Sam.

330
00:16:59,167 --> 00:17:00,433
- Sam.
- Mom.

331
00:17:00,567 --> 00:17:02,767
What did you do this time?

332
00:17:03,767 --> 00:17:05,967
- W-Wait--
- Is there a problem?

333
00:17:06,133 --> 00:17:07,900
Max, I got this.

334
00:17:08,967 --> 00:17:11,933
Sam, what happened?
Your dad is looking for you.

335
00:17:12,100 --> 00:17:15,600
When I asked why,
he wouldn't tell me.

336
00:17:15,767 --> 00:17:17,233
What's going on?

337
00:17:18,200 --> 00:17:21,133
Maybe he already got wind
of what happened.

338
00:17:21,267 --> 00:17:24,100
I wasn't planning on
hiding what I did to him.

339
00:17:24,200 --> 00:17:25,800
What did you do?

340
00:17:25,933 --> 00:17:27,500
- Well, you see--
- [RICARDO] Samantha?

341
00:17:27,667 --> 00:17:28,667
Samantha!

342
00:17:28,833 --> 00:17:33,600
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

343
00:17:33,700 --> 00:17:34,967
Dad...

344
00:17:35,833 --> 00:17:38,433
You broke the protocol
of your agency?!

345
00:17:38,533 --> 00:17:39,833
Is that true?!

346
00:17:40,000 --> 00:17:41,300
I want to hear it from you.

347
00:17:42,633 --> 00:17:43,467
It's true.

348
00:17:43,633 --> 00:17:45,300
No law enforcer
in their right mind

349
00:17:45,433 --> 00:17:46,800
would conduct an operation

350
00:17:46,933 --> 00:17:49,467
without his superior's
knowledge.

351
00:17:49,633 --> 00:17:51,367
You've been warned!

352
00:17:51,533 --> 00:17:53,133
But, Dad, we only did that

353
00:17:53,233 --> 00:17:55,500
to catch the members
of the gold-smuggling syndicate.

354
00:17:55,667 --> 00:17:57,800
In fact, we managed
to catch Mr. Chan!

355
00:17:57,900 --> 00:18:00,000
We're so close
to solving the case.

356
00:18:00,133 --> 00:18:01,967
You think you're that good?

357
00:18:02,067 --> 00:18:04,333
You're going against
a big syndicate.

358
00:18:04,500 --> 00:18:06,800
You're showing off at the
expense of your colleagues.

359
00:18:06,900 --> 00:18:08,167
Is that it?!

360
00:18:08,333 --> 00:18:10,167
Dad, that's not true.

361
00:18:10,967 --> 00:18:13,333
You keep saying
you'll make it up to us.

362
00:18:13,467 --> 00:18:17,300
You think ruining my name
is the best way to do so?

363
00:18:17,400 --> 00:18:21,500
Ricardo, can we talk about this
once you've calmed down?

364
00:18:21,667 --> 00:18:24,200
Ma, you don't understand.

365
00:18:24,367 --> 00:18:28,000
What she did is equivalent
to insubordination.

366
00:18:32,533 --> 00:18:35,667
Do you know the importance
of the name you're carrying?

367
00:18:35,767 --> 00:18:37,400
You're ruining my legacy!

368
00:18:40,333 --> 00:18:42,133
But I will give you
one more chance

369
00:18:43,433 --> 00:18:44,867
because your mom asked me...

370
00:18:46,233 --> 00:18:48,133
...to act more
like a father to you.

371
00:18:48,233 --> 00:18:50,367
But if you do something again
to tarnish my name,

372
00:18:51,033 --> 00:18:52,300
I won't kick you out.

373
00:18:54,233 --> 00:18:56,533
I'll forget you're my daughter.

374
00:18:56,733 --> 00:18:57,833
Ricardo!

375
00:18:57,933 --> 00:19:04,900
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

376
00:19:20,100 --> 00:19:27,067
[SOFT MUSIC PLAYING]

377
00:19:35,733 --> 00:19:36,800
[DRAWER OPENS]

378
00:19:40,633 --> 00:19:41,767
[DRAWER CLOSES]

379
00:19:42,567 --> 00:19:43,600
[SAM SIGHS]

380
00:19:51,767 --> 00:19:54,567
Maybe I should really
just drop this Zafra case.

381
00:19:57,433 --> 00:19:58,467
[SAM SIGHS]

382
00:20:03,767 --> 00:20:05,467
[INHALES DEEPLY] No.

383
00:20:07,167 --> 00:20:08,767
I can't give up on this case.

384
00:20:09,633 --> 00:20:11,267
I need to strengthen the case

385
00:20:11,267 --> 00:20:13,500
so I can hold
everyone involved accountable.

386
00:20:15,867 --> 00:20:17,067
For our nation.

387
00:20:19,533 --> 00:20:21,167
[SAM BREATHES DEEPLY]

388
00:20:21,167 --> 00:20:28,133
[SOFT MUSIC CONTINUES]

389
00:20:29,467 --> 00:20:31,500
Thank you, Gabo,
for all your help.

390
00:20:32,867 --> 00:20:35,300
If it weren't for you,

391
00:20:35,333 --> 00:20:37,533
your father wouldn't
have gotten the surgery.

392
00:20:38,233 --> 00:20:40,300
- You didn't let him down.
- [GABO SIGHS]

393
00:20:40,300 --> 00:20:41,333
Auntie,

394
00:20:41,333 --> 00:20:44,200
I wouldn't let anything bad
happen to Papa.

395
00:20:44,200 --> 00:20:46,200
I would do everything
to keep him alive.

396
00:20:46,200 --> 00:20:48,400
But really, thank you so much.

397
00:20:48,400 --> 00:20:50,767
I don't know what I'd do
if we lost your dad.

398
00:20:51,633 --> 00:20:53,200
[VOICE SHAKING] Thank you, Gabo.

399
00:20:54,133 --> 00:20:55,267
Auntie Betchay...

400
00:20:58,133 --> 00:21:01,700
I lost my mother
at an early age.

401
00:21:03,400 --> 00:21:06,900
I can't lose Papa either.

402
00:21:06,900 --> 00:21:11,467
[GENTLE MUSIC PLAYING]

403
00:21:11,500 --> 00:21:12,933
[WHEELS RATTLING]

404
00:21:12,933 --> 00:21:14,633
Oh, there he is. There he is.

405
00:21:17,167 --> 00:21:18,233
- Rudy.
- Pa.

406
00:21:19,433 --> 00:21:20,467
How are you feeling?

407
00:21:22,867 --> 00:21:24,433
[NURSE] Excuse me.

408
00:21:24,433 --> 00:21:26,233
Nurse, please be gentle.
He might get hurt.

409
00:21:27,267 --> 00:21:28,433
Come on, slowly.

410
00:21:28,433 --> 00:21:30,233
- Gently.
- Gently, please.

411
00:21:30,233 --> 00:21:31,533
- [NURSE] Get up slowly, sir.
- Slowly, Pa.

412
00:21:32,367 --> 00:21:33,833
[NURSE] Slowly, sir.

413
00:21:33,833 --> 00:21:35,433
Slowly, Pa.

414
00:21:35,433 --> 00:21:37,600
- [MAMENG] Don't hurry.
- Slowly, slowly.

415
00:21:37,600 --> 00:21:38,800
[GABO] Slowly, Pa.

416
00:21:40,400 --> 00:21:42,367
There you go.

417
00:21:42,400 --> 00:21:43,733
[RUDY BREATHES DEEPLY]

418
00:21:48,900 --> 00:21:50,267
How do you feel?

419
00:21:51,633 --> 00:21:52,667
A bit...

420
00:21:53,900 --> 00:21:55,667
better, son.

421
00:21:58,800 --> 00:21:59,900
Don't worry, Pa.

422
00:22:00,800 --> 00:22:02,233
You'll be discharged soon.

423
00:22:19,267 --> 00:22:20,633
[BETCHAY] Oh, Doc.

424
00:22:20,633 --> 00:22:23,333
- Good day.
- How's it going? Any updates?

425
00:22:23,333 --> 00:22:25,800
The patient's stats
and progress are good.

426
00:22:25,800 --> 00:22:27,833
We're expecting
a quick recovery.

427
00:22:27,833 --> 00:22:29,833
And if this continues,

428
00:22:29,833 --> 00:22:31,400
he can go home in no time.

429
00:22:32,000 --> 00:22:34,900
Doctor, can we take him home
so he can recover there?

430
00:22:34,900 --> 00:22:36,267
You can do that.

431
00:22:36,267 --> 00:22:37,933
You just need
to sign the waiver.

432
00:22:37,933 --> 00:22:39,933
- I'll get going.
- Thank you.

433
00:22:41,467 --> 00:22:43,833
Pa, did you hear that?

434
00:22:43,833 --> 00:22:45,500
You will be home soon.

435
00:22:45,500 --> 00:22:46,600
You know what,

436
00:22:46,600 --> 00:22:49,800
Gabo managed to get money
to pay for your surgery.

437
00:22:58,633 --> 00:22:59,833
Son, I want to go home.

438
00:23:02,433 --> 00:23:04,500
Uh, sure. I'll pack your things.

439
00:23:04,500 --> 00:23:07,267
- I'll go handle the paperwork.
- Yes.

440
00:23:07,267 --> 00:23:08,500
Come on, come on.

441
00:23:08,500 --> 00:23:09,667
Let's go, Dante.

442
00:23:11,533 --> 00:23:12,767
[GABO SIGHS]

443
00:23:12,767 --> 00:23:19,667
[GENTLE MUSIC CONTINUES]

444
00:23:25,467 --> 00:23:26,500
I am so happy that your
surgery went well,

445
00:23:26,667 --> 00:23:29,000
and I hope that your recovery
goes smoothly.

446
00:23:31,633 --> 00:23:33,867
Gabo, tell me the truth.

447
00:23:36,133 --> 00:23:38,033
Did you do anything
illegal?

448
00:23:38,167 --> 00:23:39,867
Where did you get the money?

449
00:23:40,000 --> 00:23:42,200
[MOROSE MUSIC PLAYING]

450
00:23:42,333 --> 00:23:43,633
No, Pa.

451
00:23:45,133 --> 00:23:47,000
I took on a job...

452
00:23:48,033 --> 00:23:50,033
and that's where
I got the money.

453
00:23:50,167 --> 00:23:52,000
It's from a job
that I did.

454
00:23:52,967 --> 00:23:55,000
I accepted it to have
money for your surgery.

455
00:23:56,067 --> 00:24:01,467
What exactly did you do
to get that money?

456
00:24:01,600 --> 00:24:04,500
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

457
00:24:04,600 --> 00:24:07,033
Someone asked me to do
a job for them.

458
00:24:09,033 --> 00:24:11,300
He was a fellow inmate.

459
00:24:12,933 --> 00:24:14,733
I was surprised...

460
00:24:17,200 --> 00:24:19,300
when I saw him
and his group.

461
00:24:20,267 --> 00:24:22,867
They were the ones
who gave me the job.

462
00:24:23,000 --> 00:24:24,900
They asked me...

463
00:24:25,933 --> 00:24:27,567
to get something
for them.

464
00:24:31,367 --> 00:24:33,400
I was paid to get gold.

465
00:24:33,533 --> 00:24:36,900
That's how I was able
to pay for your surgery.

466
00:24:37,033 --> 00:24:38,067
Gold?

467
00:24:38,200 --> 00:24:42,900
[MOROSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

468
00:24:43,033 --> 00:24:44,700
I'll be honest, Pa.

469
00:24:46,967 --> 00:24:48,667
When I got the gold...

470
00:24:52,600 --> 00:24:54,567
I had second thoughts...

471
00:24:56,633 --> 00:24:58,900
about giving it
to them.

472
00:24:59,033 --> 00:25:00,733
The truth is...

473
00:25:01,433 --> 00:25:05,367
that gold can change
our lives.

474
00:25:06,500 --> 00:25:08,700
We can live
a lavish life, Pa.

475
00:25:09,800 --> 00:25:12,367
We can buy anything
we want.

476
00:25:13,833 --> 00:25:14,933
But, Pa...

477
00:25:17,500 --> 00:25:18,967
I felt guilty.

478
00:25:20,267 --> 00:25:21,967
And I thought of you.

479
00:25:23,633 --> 00:25:27,900
Even though I knew I won't
earn that much...

480
00:25:29,333 --> 00:25:31,467
I decided to
do the right thing.

481
00:25:32,333 --> 00:25:34,100
It made me think
of you, Pa.

482
00:25:35,367 --> 00:25:36,833
You did that?

483
00:25:37,667 --> 00:25:40,133
You gave up the gold?

484
00:25:40,267 --> 00:25:42,833
Please don't be mad
at me.

485
00:25:43,000 --> 00:25:45,500
I did it because I knew
it was the right thing to do.

486
00:25:46,967 --> 00:25:48,000
I'm not mad.

487
00:25:49,167 --> 00:25:51,567
I'm so happy
to hear that.

488
00:25:53,467 --> 00:25:54,933
I'm very happy.

489
00:25:56,033 --> 00:26:00,333
[HOPEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

490
00:26:00,467 --> 00:26:01,667
Pa...

491
00:26:02,467 --> 00:26:04,500
I know we'll get
through this.

492
00:26:05,467 --> 00:26:07,600
I know that no matter
what happens,

493
00:26:07,700 --> 00:26:10,100
and whatever challenges
we face...

494
00:26:11,500 --> 00:26:14,467
we can overcome
all of them.

495
00:26:14,567 --> 00:26:15,700
[EXHALES SHARPLY]

496
00:26:22,067 --> 00:26:23,467
Thank you, son.

497
00:26:25,467 --> 00:26:32,500
[HOPEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

498
00:26:44,267 --> 00:26:47,500
<i>If you find that treasure,
we'll split it between us.</i>

499
00:26:47,667 --> 00:26:48,467
<i> Rudy took everything!</i>

500
00:26:48,600 --> 00:26:51,200
<i>I told you not to trust
that bastard!</i>

501
00:26:51,367 --> 00:26:52,167
<i> Find him.</i>

502
00:26:52,333 --> 00:26:54,500
<i>I don't care
wherever he is!</i>

503
00:26:54,600 --> 00:26:55,500
<i> If you come with me,</i>

504
00:26:57,367 --> 00:26:59,333
The conflict of the past...

505
00:26:59,500 --> 00:27:02,667
<i>That gold is the reason
we lost everything.</i>

506
00:27:02,767 --> 00:27:06,367
...will bring chaos
to the present.

507
00:27:06,533 --> 00:27:08,500
<i>He has to pay
for what he did to my mother.</i>

508
00:27:08,600 --> 00:27:09,400
<i> I need to find him!</i>
